From a0b45e3375a98ecfa618e055750e0d30706bfc76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: song <songyiqiang1994@163.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 08:55:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/20] fix: audit commit 6 review - use positional key
 matching for encryption

CRITICAL: auditArgIsKey used value-based strcmp matching, which
incorrectly treats non-key arguments as keys when their content
happens to match a key name (e.g. SET key key would not encrypt
the value). This violates the design spec which requires keys to
be identified by position, not by value.

- auditExtractKeys: added int **key_positions output parameter
  recording the argv index of each extracted key
- auditFreeKeys: updated to free key_positions array
- auditBuildCommandParam: replaced auditArgIsKey (value matching)
  with auditArgIsKeyByPosition (argv index matching)
- Updated debug.c: DEBUG AUDIT-KEYS and DEBUG AUDIT-PARAM callers
- Added 2 regression tests: value=key-name encrypted, RENAME with
  duplicate key names
---
 src/audit.c              | 61 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 src/audit.h              |  7 +++--
 src/debug.c              | 12 +++++---
 tests/unit/audit-log.tcl | 11 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 64 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

